<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3>Is a Home Business Policy more expensive than a standard Homeowner’s Policy?</h3>
<p>This may depend on the specific coverage required for your business. While a Home Business Policy generally provides more extensive coverage and therefore might be more expensive, it’s crucial to consider the potential financial risk of not having adequate coverage for your home-based business.</p>
<h3>How often should I review my home business insurance coverage?</h3>
<p>We recommend reviewing your policy annually or whenever significant changes occur in your business. Changes could include the purchase of new equipment, hiring employees, or expanding your service offerings.</p>
<h3>Does a Business Owners Policy (BOP) cover employees who work from my home?</h3>
<p>A BOP typically covers employees in terms of liability. If you have employees regularly working from your home, you should discuss this with your insurance agent to ensure you have the right coverage.</p>
<h3>What if I have multiple businesses run from my home?</h3>
<p>If you run more than one business from your home, each business may present unique risks and therefore may require separate coverage. Discuss your specific situation with your insurance agent to determine the best coverage for your needs.</p>
<h3>Do I need a home business insurance if I am only working from home temporarily?</h3>
<p>If you are temporarily working from home due to circumstances such as a global pandemic, you may not require a home business policy. However, if you have brought home high-value company equipment, it’s important to confirm with your employer’s business insurance provider if the equipment will be covered in case of loss or damage.</p>
